event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":85,"item_id":"rs_021928b8a7a7325f016acd1d0ebe5887d2915dfff23be51326","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering test files**\n\nI'm thinking about whether I need to append tests through a new separate file or if I can reuse helpers in the same test file by editing the end. I’m wondering if a new test file would work better, especially if the helper isn’t exported yet. It seems like I should prepend new tests before any existing ones to keep everything unique and organized. I guess that could end up being around 100 lines."}

